# PANOSETI Control GUI Environment Configuration (.env.example)
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in your working directory (or wherever you run
# pseti-gui from) to customize GUI behavior without exporting variables in
# your shell profile.
#
# `pseti-gui` automatically loads `.env` from the current working directory
# at startup -- see pseti_gui.env_loader.load_pseti_gui_env(). To point at a
# specific file instead:
#   PSETI_GUI_ENV_FILE=/path/to/my-site.env pseti-gui
#
# Values are plain `KEY=value` (no `export`) -- this file is parsed directly
# by python-dotenv, not sourced by a shell, so `export` is neither needed nor
# harmful either way. All values must be uncommented (remove the leading `#`)
# to take effect.

# ==============================================================================
# Image-Window Grid Configuration
# ==============================================================================
#
# Path to the window_config.json that defines the image-window grid layout
# (dimensions, and which module_id shows in which cell with what title).
# Generate a starting point with `pseti-gui --config-template`, edit it, then
# point this at your copy.
#
# Default: the packaged default layout (window_config.DEFAULT_CONFIG_PATH,
# today's 2x2 PTI/Fern/Winter/Gattini grid).
# PSETI_WINDOW_CONFIG_FILE=/path/to/window_config.json
